# The dead code gate: `make quality-check`. A finding that is not in the baseline fails, and so does a baseline entry
# that no longer matches (the code is used or gone). The baseline may only shrink: it holds what is kept on purpose,
# such as test accessors. After a change that fixes one, run `make quality-baseline`. See phpstan-dead.neon.
includes:
    - phpstan-dead.neon
    - phpstan-dead-baseline.neon
